  "body": "Follow-ups from the review of PR #3093 (#3081), comment 7053548122.\n\n1. In the refused-case rig of `a_head_tilt_past_90_under_the_table_is_refused_with_lower` (`crates/app/tests/first_traverse_table.rs`), the Z-stroke law also refuses the post. So no test shows that the new verdict `FirstTraverseUnderTable` alone blocks the post. Add a rig that stays inside the Z stroke and assert that the post error names this verdict.\n2. When the plane is above the stock top and no plane is clear, the operation shows only \"lower the clearance plane\". The \"raise\" verdict appears only after that repair. Both states refuse the post. Item 3 of `docs/decisions/3081-table-down-axis-verdict.md` says that both verdicts show: correct the wording, or show both verdicts at once.\n",
